{"kind":"request","text":"Remove spikes and realign idiosyncratic terms (Hugh, 2026-10-15 22:00 Eastern). A reviewer called the repository \"163k LOC of idiosyncratic abstraction (found/settle/duties/turns)\". Of ~182k code lines, ~78k are tests and ~47k are spikes.\n\n1. Delete all of spikes/ (parked, pi-durable, room-core, sandbox-git) from main. Before deleting, tag the last commit that has them (spikes-final) so history stays reachable. Remove every dependency on them first: apps/jam/src/phrases.ts, .github/workflows/row-writes.yml, .gitattributes, scripts (active-source.test.mjs, check-doc-links.mjs, test-changed.mjs) and docs (release.md, scopes.md, testing.md). If anything still needed lives only in spikes, move it into its owning package; say which.\n2. Rename \"found\" to \"create\" everywhere it means making a scope: the public SDK (client/src/handle.ts found(), foundingOffer, founding-offer.ts), CLI commands and help, MCP tools, internal identifiers (foundedKind, foundingObjects, foundingOf, Core#found and the rest), comments and docs. No compatibility aliases. \"Founder\" as a role may become \"creator\" in prose. String literals inside pinned definitions or signed/digested wire bytes (\"founder\" in directory, \"founder-key\" in register, \"founding\" in genesis, and any others) change only at that definition's next version bump; list each one in the delivery note with its file:line and the version that will carry it. Do not cut a new cohort just for wording.\n3. Replace \"duties\" with \"pending work\" in prose and \"outbox\" where it names the mechanism, in identifiers, comments and docs. It is not a pinned field; confirm that before renaming.\n4. Keep \"turn\" and \"settle\" (and the pinned settles field). Define them plainly.\n5. Add a short section \"If you know these patterns\" to docs/manual/ten-terms.md: scope = an actor with an event-sourced journal; turn = one transaction for one input; send and settle = a transactional outbox with an acknowledgement; definition = a declared state machine; create = making a scope with its genesis entry. General patterns only; no product names or comparisons.\n\nOrder: after the NOW work, alongside observability f57fc4da and capacity 113a54bd. Slices are fine (spikes removal first; it is the largest and simplest). Run the tests of what you change and the gate once per head before review. Report line counts before and after, measured by script. No push, no deploy.","body":{"conditions":"Checker approves each exact head; gate passes once per head; spikes/ gone from main with tag spikes-final; no found* identifier remains outside pinned literals, which are listed with their next versions; duties renamed; ten-terms has the patterns section; lands on local main only while the push freeze holds.","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}